{"id":"SEC-009","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-grade.sh","line":1388,"code_snippet":"def home_word_outside(): return A.executor == \"host\"","reasoning_trace":"outside() returns home_word_outside() for ~/ $HOME/ ${HOME}/ (1352); in container mode every such word is clean on the asserted ground that home is /home/evaluser. The container user and HOME are not verifiable from this PR (pipeline-run.sh and the image are out of scope). [ASSUMPTION] flagged.","finding":"~/ and $HOME/ are assumed to resolve under /home/evaluser in the container; a root or redirected HOME would be outside every allowed root and invisible to the grader","critique":"The resolution should be derived from the transcript, not asserted.","remediation":"Derive home from system/init cwd or a recorded HOME; treat ~/ as <home>/; fall back to outside when it cannot be derived; record the resolution in grade.json.","confidence":"low","references":["CWE-706"]}
